            <ArticleTitle>[Pathology of cardiac ventricular aneurysms in the horse].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>76-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The authors describe pathologic and histopathologic findings of three cardiac aneurysms in horses, two of which in the left ventricle and one in the right ventricle. The aneurysms were always associated with multiple foci of myocardiac fibrosis. A hypothesis concerning histogenesis of the lesion is formulated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
